sweaters  scarves  dresses  and even shoes at first glance this all  looks like ordinary knitwear but it  could turn out to be the forerunner of a  real revolution in the clothing industry  the items were manufactured using this  innovative machine knitter8 the world's  first fully automated professional  quality knitting machine in a compact  desktop size it was developed by gerard  rubio originally from spain he now lives  in london rubio hopes his invention will  trigger an earthquake in the fashion  industry we want to democratize clothing  manufacturing with a machine that can be  used by anyone until now clothing  manufacturing has been only in the hands  of a few skilled people and the industry  now we're providing a tool for anyone to  produce their own garments  [Music]  rubio is carrying out his assault on the  textiles industry from this office in  london's east end he met his business  partner triambak saxoner at school  knitter8 software allows users who have  no prior knowledge or experience to  create articles of clothing like a scarf  the user can determine the style and  colors themselves  my vision was to provide a tool that is  really affordable and easy to use for  people to create their own garments at  home garments that are completely  customized  and made  right in the same spot where you're  going to be wearing it  the knitting pattern is transferred to  knitter 8 on a memory card the machine  can process 6 cones of yarn  simultaneously  the carriage pulls the arm through the  feeder to the needles which then make  the stitches  knitter 8 can create garments of a  complexity and quality comparable to  those made by industrial knitting  machines and at a similar speed  so far only this prototype exists the  company raised its seed money through a  crowdfunding campaign  they were aiming for one hundred  thousand dollars but ended up raising  six hundred thousand  there are a lot of meters out there and  we've been told that this is a machine 